&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Joining our Cloud Platform team as a&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Lead DevEx Engineer, you will play a key role in improving how engineers build, ship and operate services across Liberis. This is a brand new role created to bridge the gap between application development and platform engineering - creating a more consistent, scalable developer experience as we continue to evolve our platform strategy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will focus on building for engineers - creating and shaping the templates, standards and foundations used across services. Alongside this, you will have the opportunity to contribute to emerging platform initiatives, including work that supports AI enablement across the engineering organisation.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a high-impact role with real scope to influence how engineering works at Liberis!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll get to do in the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve the service template library for .NET, Node.js, and Python — covering project&amp;nbsp;scaffolding, dependency management, containerisation, local dev setup, and production&amp;nbsp;configuration. Templates are generated, not forked, so keeping them current and opinionated&amp;nbsp;matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain CI/CD pipeline templates in GitHub Actions and/or Azure DevOps, covering build, test, security scanning, and deployment — consistent across stacks and reusable across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and ship observability standards: structured logging, distributed tracing, and alerting integrated into service templates so every new service is production-ready from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hands-on with Datadog, incident.io, and/or GCP/Azure-native logging and monitoring tooling to build the platform-level observability layer teams plug into.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to our thinking on a potential Azure-to-GCP migration — helping assess what changes for developer tooling and service templates and building proof-of-concept work that informs the&amp;nbsp;decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product engineers to understand where developer experience breaks down — slow pipelines, confusing templates, missing runbooks — and fix the root causes, not the symptoms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical decisions on platform tooling: evaluate new tools, write ADRs, and drive adoption of improvements across multiple engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers in the Cloud Platform team and act as a go-to resource for product engineers getting to grips with platform tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
